    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Here's what I found and fixed:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Broken commit:** `751f06b` (\"money: simplify the price parsers\")\n\nThe commit introduced a floating-point precision bug by replacing the safe integer-based parsing with floating-point arithmetic. When parsing \"39.95\", the calculation `39.95 * 100` results in `3995.0000000000005` instead of the exact integer `3995`.\n\n**The fix:** Restored the safe parsing approach that splits the euro and cents parts separately:\n- **Before (broken):** `Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100`\n- **After (fixed):** Split on decimal point, parse as integers, add them: `Number(euros) * 100 + Number(cents.padEnd(2, '0'))`\n\nI applied this fix to three functions:\n1. `parseEuros()` in `src/money.js`\n2. `cellCents()` in `src/money.js`  \n3. `decimalCommaToCents()` in `src/locale.js`\n\nAll 50 tests pass, and your `subtrack add Gym 39.95` command now works correctly.",
